  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});
```

Not directly a security issue, but for production deployments and containerized environments, it’s standard to use `process.env.PORT`:

```js
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`);
});
```

This also makes infrastructure configuration easier and less error‑prone.

